#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Mga kritikal na konsepto {#critical-concepts}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "the Deutsch and Deutsch-Jozsa algorithms use quantum parallelism combined with interference to find an answer to a problem faster than a classical computer can.\n"
msgstr "ang mga algorithm ng Deutsch at Deutsch-Jozsa ay gumagamit ng quantum parallelism kasama ang interference para mahanap ang sagot sa isang problema nang mas mabilis kaysa sa kayang gawin ng isang klasikal na computer.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "the phase kickback mechanism is a counterintuitive quantum phenomena that transfers operations on one qubit to the phase of another qubit. The Deutsch and Deutsch-Jozsa algorithms utilize this mechanism.\n"
msgstr "ang mekanismo ng phase kickback ay isang counterintuitive na quantum phenomena na naglilipat ng mga operasyon sa isang qubit patungo sa phase ng isa pang qubit. Ginagamit ng mga algorithm ng Deutsch at Deutsch-Jozsa ang mekanismong ito.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm offers a polynomial speedup over any deterministic classical algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Ang Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm ay nag-aalok ng polynomial na pagpapabilis kumpara sa anumang deterministic na klasikal na algorithm.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm can be applied to a different problem, called the Bernstein-Vazirani problem, to find a hidden string encoded in a function.\n"
msgstr "Ang Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm ay maaaring ilapat sa ibang problema, na tinatawag na problema ng Bernstein-Vazirani, para mahanap ang isang nakatagong string na naka-encode sa isang function.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "True/false {#truefalse}"
msgstr "Tama/Mali {#truefalse}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F Deutsch's algorithm is a special case of the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm where the input is a single qubit.\n"
msgstr "T/M Ang algorithm ni Deutsch ay isang espesyal na kaso ng Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm kung saan ang input ay isang solong qubit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The Deutsch and Deutsch-Jozsa algorithms use quantum superposition and interference to achieve their efficiency.\n"
msgstr "T/M Ang mga algorithm ng Deutsch at Deutsch-Jozsa ay gumagamit ng quantum superposisyon at interference para makamit ang kanilang kahusayan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm requires multiple function evaluations to determine if a function is constant or balanced.\n"
msgstr "T/M Ang Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm ay nangangailangan ng maraming pagsusuri ng function para matukoy kung ang isang function ay constant o balanced.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The \"Bernstein-Vazirani algorithm\" is actually the same as the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, applied to a different problem.\n"
msgstr "T/M Ang \"Bernstein-Vazirani algorithm\" ay talagang kapareho ng Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, na inilapat sa ibang problema.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The Bernstein-Vazirani algorithm can find multiple secret strings simultaneously.\n"
msgstr "T/M Ang Bernstein-Vazirani algorithm ay maaaring makahanap ng maraming lihim na string nang sabay-sabay.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Short answer {#short-answer}"
msgstr "Maikling sagot {#short-answer}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How long would it take a classical algorithm to solve the Deutsch-Jozsa problem in the worst case?\n"
msgstr "Gaano katagal ang kakailanganin ng isang klasikal na algorithm para malutas ang problema ng Deutsch-Jozsa sa pinakamasamang kaso?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How long would it take a classical algorithm to solve the Bernstein-Vazirani problem? What speedup does the DJ algorithm offer in this case?\n"
msgstr "Gaano katagal ang kakailanganin ng isang klasikal na algorithm para malutas ang problema ng Bernstein-Vazirani? Anong pagpapabilis ang inaalok ng DJ algorithm sa kasong ito?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Describe the phase-kickback mechanism and how it works to solve the Deutsch-Jozsa and Bernstein-Vazirani problems.\n"
msgstr "Ilarawan ang mekanismo ng phase-kickback at kung paano ito gumagana para malutas ang mga problema ng Deutsch-Jozsa at Bernstein-Vazirani.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Challenge problem {#challenge-problem}"
msgstr "Hamon na problema {#challenge-problem}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm: Recall that you had a question above asking you to work out the intermediate qubit states $\\pi_1$, and $\\pi_2$ of the Deutsch's algorithm. Do the same for the intermediate $n+1$-qubit states $\\pi_1$, and $\\pi_2$ of the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, for the specific case that $n=2$. Then, verify that $\\pi_3 = |-\\rangle \\otimes \\sum\\limits_{x_0...x_n}(-1)^{f(x_0...x_n)}|x_0 ... x_n\\rangle$, again, for the specific case that $n=2$.\n"
msgstr "Ang Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm: Alalahanin na mayroon kang tanong sa itaas na humihingi sa iyo na kalkulahin ang mga intermediate na estado ng qubit na $\\pi_1$, at $\\pi_2$ ng algorithm ni Deutsch. Gawin ang parehong bagay para sa mga intermediate na $(n+1)$-Qubit na estado na $\\pi_1$, at $\\pi_2$ ng Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, para sa tiyak na kaso na $n=2$. Pagkatapos, i-verify na ang $\\pi_3 = |-\\rangle \\otimes \\sum\\limits_{x_0...x_n}(-1)^{f(x_0...x_n)}|x_0 ... x_n\\rangle$, muli, para sa tiyak na kaso na $n=2$.\n"
